#
# The symbols the core's objects need that nothing in this repository
# defines, one per line, as the linker prints them (libstdc++ names).
# build/build.py fails when the set changes. It is empty: the five base::
# functions that upstream defines in the Windows-only client/compat/base.cc
# (Base64Encode, Base64Decode, NumberToString for int, long and double) are
# defined in port/base. Do not add a line to make a build pass; a new
# undefined symbol means the core gained a dependency that needs a decision.
